  "reason": "The current best is config_038 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) at 0.721 accuracy, a strong jump over the best RNA-only (0.653). The evidence clearly shows: (1) scvi_n200 is the best RNA encoder, (2) multiprofile is essential, (3) imagenet_vit_l is the strongest image encoder, and (4) multimodal fusion provides a substantial boost. The key remaining uncertainty within this winning configuration is the fusion method: concat (tested, 0.721) vs. weighted (untested). Config_039 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted, isolating this single design choice. This is the cleanest and most informative next experiment: if weighted fusion improves accuracy, we gain a new best with 2 experiments left to confirm; if it does not, we confirm concat is optimal and can spend remaining budget on other refinements. With only 2 experiments remaining, this minimal-change comparison is the highest-value use of the next slot."
